# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_auth_lifecycle.py" "AUTH LIFECYCLE GATE: PASS" "auth lifecycle" "auth lifecycle (token expiry/revocation recovery, bounded rate-limit retry, content-free secrets)" "auth lifecycle (installation-token under stress: early-revocation 401 remints+retries-once everywhere INCL. the tarball ingest; a 403 STALE-CREDENTIAL (a mid-life token invalidation -- a permission re-approval during a migration) ALSO remints+retries-once, while a GENUINE permission 403 (Resource not accessible by integration) does NOT remint-loop and a rate-limit 403 is NOT mistaken for a stale credential; proactive refresh w/o herd; rate-limit burst bounded; read-then-write 401 no double-act; NO secret ever in a log/exception)" 28
